uncharted 4 launched in May and the  multiplayer side of Nathan Drake's final  adventure is still going strong in fact  the first multiplayer DLC pack is out  right now lost treasures comes to  uncharted 4 via the games 1 point 0 8  update which means everyone gets it for  free lost treasures brings a ton of new  content including the small arena like  sunken ruins map there are also several  new weapons and boosters plus a new path  of Indra mystical which lets you  teleport to any Ally tons of new vanity  items can be found in the store to over  50 new skins and 70 new hat and face  items to be exact the patch itself also  adds a new leveling system to  multiplayer with each rank earning you  unique items it also revamps ranked team  deathmatch to make the mode run in  seasons a few balance changes and weapon  fixes are also baked into the update  lost treasures is the first of four  plans multiplayer DLC packs for  uncharted 4 with the others coming this  autumn winter 2017 and spring 2017  developer Naughty Dog has also mentioned  single-player DLC but currently has  nothing to announce when they do you can  be sure you'll hear about it from  GameSpot
 

